# Review

## Summary

The note cites no external studies or empirical results. Its supports are Commonplace theory and reference notes about the same domain: KB note selection, curation and writing. The one general principle applied to a specific case is "weakly discriminated qualities tend to be underselected". The note marks it as a conjecture ("Under the conjecture that") and states the bridging condition just before it: existing gates discriminate validity more strongly than learning value. Because that mechanism is stated, the transfer to autonomous authoring is explicit and conditional, not unbridged.
